# DTF tier manifest: index-metadata-cred-scoping
#   (GHSA-24rf-2gv2-j47c, fixed in 1.11.0 by artifact-keeper #4588)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams.mock-index-foreign (two stdlib
# hosts on a per-slot 172.16/12 subnet: `mock-idx`, the configured upstream,
# whose PyPI simple page and Helm index.yaml name files by absolute URL on
# itself or on `mock-foreign`; both record every Authorization header).
#
# THE BUG
# The shared upstream fetchers attached a Remote's configured Basic or Bearer
# credentials to whatever URL they were given, including download URLs taken
# from index metadata (PyPI href, Helm urls, Cargo dl, Composer dist.url,
# Terraform download_url). A hostile or compromised index could name a host it
# controls and receive the credentials, triggered by any client, anonymous
# ones included on a public Remote. The fix attaches credentials only when the
# request URL has the scheme, host and port of `upstream_url` (or
# `index_upstream_url`); any other URL is still fetched, without credentials,
# and a sampled `security` WARN is logged.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: red on ak-backend:1.10.0 (4 FIX cases: PyPI href Basic, Helm
# urls Basic, anonymous public PyPI Bearer, the WARN), green on 1.11.0 and on
# today's main. CONTROLS (green on both): the index documents and same-origin
# files keep the credentials; a cross-origin 302 is followed with
# Authorization stripped by the HTTP client (the advisory notes redirects were
# already safe); no secret in the backend log.
#
# The public Remote is created with allow_public_with_upstream_credentials
# (#4662, 1.11.1) so it is accepted on new images; older ones ignore it.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~15 calls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock hosts are on a private subnet.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-index-foreign"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
